  "id": "cross-modal-association",
  "term": "cross-modal association",
  "definition": "Cross-modal association is the linking of information from one sense with processing usually related to another sense. In the source example, tactile input during Braille reading or shape discrimination by the mouth was associated with activity in parietal and occipital cortical areas, suggesting shared tactile-visual processing.",
